  "id": "COMPOUND:36187 - PROTEIN:6323",
  "verbalization": "Isohalitulin is implicated in the regulation of DNA polymerase iota through a multi-step mechanism involving histone deacetylase 5. This enzyme is a target of multiple compounds, including Eupachinilide A and Epigallocatechin 7-O-gallate, which in turn target DNA polymerase iota. The evidence suggests that Isohalitulin may exert its effects by modulating histone deacetylase 5, which could influence the activity of DNA polymerase iota. The shared target of multiple compounds and the presence of a direct link between Isohalitulin and DNA polymerase iota indicate a potential regulatory pathway where Isohalitulin may act as a modulator of the activity of DNA polymerase iota through histone deacetylase 5. The integration of these pathways highlights the possibility of a broader regulatory network involving histone deacetylase 5 and DNA polymerase iota, underscoring the role of histone deacetylase 5 as a critical mediator in this relationship.",
